ask's topology premise\",\"status\":\"partially_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Discovery (tcpdump/ping probes) found the authored transit/lan-a/lan-b segments non-functional at the addressing level — node1's eth1, node2's vtnet1/vtnet2, and node4's enp8s0 showed no reachable peer traffic, contradicting the intended segmented topology in node_images/nics. The executor worked around this by adding a host-specific route on node3 (via node1) and a matching static route on node1 (via node2) over the flat management subnet, plus disabling ICMP send-redirects on node1 to stop node3 bypassing it. The matching IP-IDs at node1 and node2 for the same packet prove the forced path worked for this specific flow, but this is an engineered workaround over the mgmt network rather than confirmation that the originally authored dedicated-network topology functions as described.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c14f46a80f804d53\",\"cmd-a8e24bddcdb149bb\",\"cmd-1eb51345101f40d3\",\"cmd-ab0b6ba7de2048ed\",\"cmd-02ca75eed3424d84\",\"cmd-97e2a81d585e4ff4\",\"cmd-4c123a9cb33d4753\",\"cmd-af86afb239964264\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-evidence-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on every managed node with pre/post boot identity, healthy baseline, and recovered state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"All four nodes show a pre-restart boot identity/state, a restart acknowledgement, a distinct post-restart boot identity matching the fixed after-executor snapshot, and recovery of relevant state: node1 (route, firewall rule, send_redirects), node2 (pf rule, forwarding, plus a fresh correlated log pair), node3 (persistent route, blocked-attempt re-verified), node4 (interface address). A final full-chain attempt after all four restarts reproduced the matching permit/refuse log pair (ID 32170/32171), corroborating full recovery.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-46ad6a37861f490d\",\"cmd-ce76bcff0cde46cb\",\"cmd-9d579f7e86004b61\",\"cmd-75423a12804a4fcd\",\"cmd-2f3d6eb154c24